"""Runtime for Python code generated by `macropress convert`.

The generated code calls these helpers so that it keeps VBA's and Excel's behaviour:
VBA comparisons and arithmetic (Empty, type conversion), variables with declared types,
ByRef arguments, and the Excel model (sheets, ranges, selection, filters, copy/paste).
Needs the Python standard library, and lxml to save the workbook. Not vb2py.

In generated code:
    xl      the workbook session: xl.Range(...), xl.Selection, xl.Sheets(...), xl.Err ...
    v       the variables of the running procedure: v.co_counter
    rt.X    VBA built-in functions (rt.Left, rt.Mid, rt.Now ...) and constants (rt.xlDown)
"""

